# Release signing material. `keystore.properties` holds the store path and the
# two passwords, and the store itself is a *.jks next to the project (see
# keystore.properties.example). Neither may ever be committed: a leaked signing
# key cannot be rotated for an app that is already installed, only for a new
# applicationId. The example file IS committed; it carries no values.
keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
